:5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0095. I couldn't find anything that blocks it, and none of the TEP-0004 rejection triggers applies.\n\n**Last rejection (scope, rule R2):** fixed. The fork's commits for this packet are `b094a63`, which added the stray `sdkjs-forms` clone, and `2262b2e`, which reverts it. `git -C external/sdkjs diff refs/theseus/base..HEAD` is now empty, so the contract's \"no change to the code of sdkjs\" holds. The guard in `build.sh` that adds `/.theseus-addons/` to the checkout's local exclude list is idempotent and doesn't touch any tracked file. It is a little odd for the build step of one oracle to change a checkout's git settings, but it is local and justified.\n\n**Scope and budget:** all seven new files are in `.theseus/oracle/differential`, about 375 diff lines against a limit of 1500. The diff touches 9 files against a limit of 8, but two of those are the packet file and `friction.jsonl`, which the method itself requires. The factory has already passed scope.\n\n**Goal:** met.\n- Both scripts compare the original and new sdkjs, each built from its source and cached by content in `$THESEUS_CACHE_DIR`.\n- The editor runs in Chromium against the live server, with two users so co-editing is real.\n- The run covers scripted local edits by user A and remote edits by user B, then save, reopen and convert.\n- It compares the model, what each user sent to the other, what the screen shows, the reopened document and the converted file.\n- A `.intended` file sits next to each script for intended differences, and each case prints one timing line for both sides.\n\n**Strong points:**\n- A guard fails a case when the scripted edits are not in the final document. Before it existed, a case could pass with no edit at all, and it caught `chart.pptx` doing exactly that.\n- The executor ran a mutation check: a bundle that changes typed text was caught in five of the six checks and the script exited 1. The sixth (what B sent) could not change, because B types no 'n'.\n- Every way the two sides' outputs can drift on their own is explained in the log. Paragraph ids are random, and batching of sent changes depends on timing.\n\n**Weaknesses, none blocking:**\n1. **The saved file is not compared directly.** `savedBytes` is computed in `run.cjs` but never compared. The saved document is checked only through the reopened model dump, which is fairly shallow: text, line counts, bold and font size for Word; shape position and text for slides. A change that only shows in formatting or in the XML could pass. A follow-up could compare the saved files after unzipping them and normalizing the ids.\n2. **Narrow coverage.** No case edits a chart object remotely, which the log states. The edits are text plus one bold run.\n3. **Timing shows no gain.** About 4.3 s to open and 3 s to edit on both sides, with noise of the same size, so the timing lines don't yet show any speed-up.\n4. **The checks differ by file type.** For `.pptx` the \"converted\" check compares a model dump of the reopened ODP file; for `.docx` it compares a hash of the TXT output.\n\nNo follow-up packets were requested, so the empty Spawned packets section is consistent.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Differential oracle meets the goal with a working edit-landed guard and a mutation check; the fork's net diff is empty again, so the scope violation is fixed.","ttft_ms":2343,"type":"result","duration_ms":23368,"uuid":"3cc6b903-bf48-4261-a0ca-d219f1718d7e","ttft_stream_ms":1070,"time_to_request_ms":406,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":12,"system_prompt":274,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":18,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":10,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":12,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":7,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":25,"mess